  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The general election for Oregon's 4th Congressional District pits incumbent Democratic Rep. Val Hoyle against Republican challenger Monique DeSpain in a rematch of the 2024 election. The district covers Lane County (including Eugene and Springfield), the central and southern Oregon coast, and parts of Douglas County, and has a slight Democratic lean. Hoyle is seeking a third term after defeating DeSpain by nearly eight points in 2024, while DeSpain is making her second bid for the seat. The race offers voters a clear contrast between Hoyle's progressive record on labor and reproductive rights and DeSpain's conservative focus on public safety, border security, and economic affordability.",
